      "answer": {
        "schema_version": "grounded-answer-v1",
        "answer_id": "ans_ecd3c87b040a4e4083c54eb2fcb2db0f",
        "run_id": "run_e9e24ee1b3ff41e1887f239d69bb62f9",
        "answer_markdown": "The model’s strongest highlighted features are distributed across the molecule rather than confined to one fragment: the tertiary amine (`N`), ether oxygen (`O`), and the sulfonamide-containing aryl regions, especially the sulfur atoms. The attribution ranks the tertiary amine highest by magnitude, followed by the ether oxygen and sulfonamide sulfur atoms. These are model-input highlights, not a validated binding pharmacophore.\n\nThe hERG model classifies this molecule as a blocker.\n\nNo. This attribution does not establish how dofetilide blocks the channel. It indicates which tokens moved this model’s score; it does not demonstrate channel binding, pore interaction, state dependence, or blocking mechanism. The explainer’s own validation found the highlighted atoms were not more faithful than random-atom deletion, so the structural interpretation should be treated as weak and hypothesis-generating.",
        "claims": [
          {
            "claim_id": "clm_8f4a2d9c7b1e6a3d5c0e9f2b4a7d1c6e",
            "kind": "classification",
            "text": "The hERG model classifies the molecule as a blocker.",
            "transform": "identity",
            "citation_ids": [],
            "observation_id": "obs_c244e72586d54bfcb14392ee87fb24bf",
            "field_path": "predictions.herg.label",
            "source_value": "blocker"
          },
          {
            "claim_id": "clm_b7e1d4a9c3f0628e5b6d1a7f4c9e2b30",
            "kind": "scientific",
            "text": "The attribution highlights the tertiary amine, ether oxygen, and sulfonamide-containing aryl regions, with the tertiary amine highest by attribution magnitude among the listed tokens.",
            "transform": "identity",
            "citation_ids": [],
            "observation_id": "obs_10db0dfaf1b541dea961c6ea0027771a",
            "field_path": "top_tokens"
          },
          {
            "claim_id": "clm_4c9a7e2d1f6b8e3a0d5c7f2b9a6e1d43",
            "kind": "limitation",
            "text": "Attribution identifies features that moved the model score, not a causal channel-blocking mechanism; its reported faithfulness validation was not better than random control.",
